## Edge cases, recovery policies, gates, and audit artifacts

### Edge cases and handling

The table below lists the edge cases that most often break prompt-only migration systems and the required handling policy. Where official framework behavior matters, the handling is anchored in those sources; where no single source exists, the response is a conservative design recommendation.

| Edge case | Detection evidence | Responsible agent / skill | Required handling |
|---|---|---|---|
| Maven multi-module reactor | aggregator POM, parent relationships, reactor convergence risk | `discovery` + `build-graph` | separate aggregation from inheritance; never assume root-only build means isolated scope |
| Gradle composite builds | `includeBuild`, included builds, convention plugins | `discovery` + `build-graph` | model included builds separately; do not patch across composite boundaries in one batch |
| Generated code | annotation processors, generated-sources, codegen plugins | `discovery` + `build-graph` | classify as generated; patch source definitions, not generated output |
| Shared modules with hidden business logic | `common/core/shared/platform` packages containing entities/services/repos | `service-boundary` + `ownership-map` | treat as business-relevant until ownership is proven; block extraction if ownership remains ambiguous |
| Ambiguous ownership | one table or workflow touched by many modules without authoritative owner | `service-boundary` | emit `BLOCKED`; require ownership decision before extraction |
| Transactional boundaries | `@Transactional`, transaction-bound events, nested service calls | `architecture` + `runtime-semantics` | freeze the boundary; prefer same-language extraction or facade-first isolation |
| Eventual consistency paths | async listeners, outbox, message relays, batch jobs | `architecture` + `data-cutover` | use outbox/CDC or replay-capable event baselines; never assume sync semantics |
| Async and scheduled work | `@Async`, `@Scheduled`, MVC async return types | `discovery` + `runtime-semantics` | create separate equivalence checks for timing, retries, and thread behavior |
| External integrations | HTTP clients, messaging adapters, Spring Integration endpoints | `architecture` + `api-freeze` | baseline request/response/event schemas and failure behavior before moving code |
| Secrets and config resolution | externalized config, env vars, Vault refs, profile-specific properties | `discovery` + `runtime-semantics` | never invent values; unresolved production secrets remain `UNSPECIFIED` and block readiness |
| Missing tests | no characterization or contract coverage on changed path | `planner` + `test-strength` | require characterization tests before risky change; no “green by absence” allowed |
| Large repo token limits | monorepo, many modules, huge generated files | all agents | process by build root, module, package, and contract boundary; summarize into artifacts between turns |
| Security chain sensitivity | `SecurityFilterChain`, custom filters, method security | `architecture` + `stabilization` | preserve authn/authz order and security tests; block cutover without parity |
| Async event publication after commit | `@TransactionalEventListener` and outbox/event bridges | `architecture` + `data-cutover` | verify commit-phase semantics and downstream timing before route movement |

Spring’s transaction, event, async, scheduling, and security documentation is why these edge cases are not optional details: they materially change behavior. Spring Boot’s external configuration and Actuator also make config and operational parity first-order migration concerns. citeturn0search4turn0search12turn7search1turn3search3turn3search15turn8search0turn2search3turn1search3

### Failure classification and recovery

| Failure class | Typical trigger | Owner | Recovery policy |
|---|---|---|---|
| `STATIC_FAILURE` | missing imports, package drift, stale references | `stabilization` | repair current patch only |
| `BUILD_FAILURE` | reactor break, plugin failure, config mismatch | `stabilization` | fix build root first; do not continue feature work |
| `TEST_FAILURE` | broken unit/slice/integration/security test | `stabilization` | add characterization if behavior was unclear, then repair |
| `FUNCTIONAL_DRIFT` | same inputs, different outputs or side effects | `implementation` then `stabilization` | revert or facade the change; do not normalize drift |
| `MUTATION_WEAKNESS` | surviving critical mutants | `mutation` | strengthen tests, do not waive silently |
| `OBSERVABILITY_GAP` | missing health, metric, trace, log parity | `architecture` then `stabilization` | block cutover until restored |
| `DB_RISK` | destructive DDL, unsafe backfill, orphaned ownership | `architecture` + `planner` | roll back to expand/contract or stop |
| `DRIFT_DETECTED` | repo changed outside recorded plan | `reload-state` | block and refresh baselines |
| `STALLED` | same normalized failure after three repair attempts | `stabilization` | emit root-cause report and stop |
| `OSCILLATION` | fixes alternate between two failure states | `stabilization` | revert last patch, isolate a smaller scope |

